A||||6||BAM-BAM||Help me out here.....PLEASE!!||||5||
Z||000000||BAM-BAM||10-18-2001||08:33 PM||||  I was given an 86 2.8 Fiero engine, complete. The block only has about 4,000 miles max (so I was told) and it looks as though it's relatively new. The problem was that the guy that gave it to me said that it had over heated, when he checked the oil there was water in it. So he immediately pulled the motor. Replaced it with a junk yard motor because he didn't want to take the time to tear it all down (didn't have the time). Ok, so I tear the plenum. middle intake and the lower intake off. What I find is that the intake manifold gasket was torn at what looks to be a water jacket. Now I have never worked with this kind of stuff so I could be wrong. My thinking is that water seeped (or poured) down into the valley and on down through the cam and such. Is this a possibility? If so, what do I do to rectify this oil/water dilemma? Any help is greatly appreciated. TIA<P><BR>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||ssalyers||10-18-2001||08:50 PM||||It's already out, buy a good head set (gaskets) and replace all the upper-end gaskets (head gaskets etc...) and you'll have an engine that's like new.  To my knowledege the 2.8's were not prone to head warpage or cracking.  You might consider some performace upgrades (cam etc..) while it's out.  Just my two pennies!!!!||||reg||4
Z||000002||ironhedno3||10-18-2001||08:58 PM||||yes it is possible for seepage at the intake gasket as you said..very common on the 60 degree v6..an ironhead 2.8/3.1/3.4 will snap a head bolt before they crack heads||||reg||1
Z||000003||tgowens||10-19-2001||12:00 AM||||Well........... that, more than likely could be the problem but..... if it were me, I would go ahead and pull the heads and take them to a machine shop and have them checked. It would be a shame to put that engine back together just to find the same problems. What you should have done before tearing into it would have been to hook up a battery pack and remote starter and crank it over and check the compression on each cylinder.<P>Now, not to correct ssalyers or ironhedno3 but we get Fieros in here (Fiero Shop) all the time with one or both heads cracked. It is a fairly common thing on the 2.8. <I>If</I> the engine only has 4,000 miles on it and it is from an 86 it has more than likely been rebuilt. Think of it this way, why would someone pull an engine out of an 86 with only 4,000 miles on it??<P>Do yourself a big favor and have the heads checked while you are down there - then replace the head gaskets and the intake gaskets and you should be good to go.<P>Call me if you have any questions........||||reg||1
Z||000004||ray b||10-19-2001||12:18 AM||||you can do a leak down, test compressed air into cyl and listen to hear if it is going out valves or pasted rings ect and how long it will hold pressure. air bottle or small tyre tipe air comp will work or turn it over by hand and ck compression [not as good as runing test but]<BR><P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000005||Wannabe||10-19-2001||01:05 AM||||Overheating is a quick way to toast even the most bulletproof engine. A leakdown and comp test will be a good idea, or at least take a close look at the condition of the cylinder walls if or when you get the heads off. Watery oil will quickly grow sludge. Make sure to flush everything out before you run the engine to full temp.||||reg||1
Z||000006||BAM-BAM||10-19-2001||06:47 AM||||  Thanks for all the input, it is truly appreciated. <BR>  Terry, the I should have been more specific. The block was replaced with a reman.. and only had 4,000 miles. The guy just didn't have the time to tear into it and replaced the entire unit with an engine out of a wrecked Fiero. Since then he got rid of the Fiero and the woman who owned it  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> My intentions were to tear it down and have it checked out, have the heads reworked, have it over bored and put it into my sons 87GT. Possibly with a turbo. I just needed to know if my diagnosis was at least in the warm range or if I was just that mechanically challenged. Again I thank you all for your input.<P>Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
